====================================================================
OBSERVATIONS
====================================================================

1. **Determinism fix is live.**
   `data_edges_sorted` replaced the HashSet-iteration data-collection
   in `discover_motifs`, `find_instances_of`, and
   `refine_candidates`. Output is now stable across process runs,
   not merely within one run. Previously, the same seed with the
   same data produced different outputs between runs because
   `HashSet<R>` iteration order is randomized per-HashMap. The
   sorted data makes the PRNG's selection deterministic end-to-end.

2. **On the canonical mixed graph with seed 2024, discover_motifs
   happens to produce all-clean representatives.**
   The representatives picked (first-sample-per-canonical) are:
   - 2-chain → `{R(c2,c3), R(c3,c4)}`  (clean chain interior)
   - 2-star → `{R(s,sa), R(s,sb)}`      (clean star subset)
   - 3-chain → `{R(c1,c2), R(c2,c3), R(c3,c4)}`  (clean)
   - 3-cycle → `{R(k1,k2), R(k2,k3), R(k3,k1)}`  (clean, because
     participants induce exactly the cycle)
   - 3-tree → `{R(t1,t2), R(t1,t3), R(t2,t4)}`  (clean tree)
   - 3-star → `{R(s,sa), R(s,sb), R(s,sc)}`      (clean star)
   Refinement is therefore a no-op on all of them — each candidate's
   `is_clean_subgraph(representative) == true`, so the early-exit
   branch in `refine_candidates` fires.
   This is the expected outcome when sampling happens to hit clean
   instances first. It's not a bug — it's why the explicit demo
   below exists.

3. **Explicit demo confirms refinement works when needed.**
   Constructed a 2-chain `MotifCandidate` with representative
   `{R(k1,k2), R(k3,k1)}` — structurally a 2-chain (canonicalizes
   to `[(1, 2), (2, 0)]`) but participants `{k1, k2, k3}` induce
   3 data edges (the full 3-cycle), not 2 — so not clean.
   `refine_candidates` with `max_tries = 200` returned
   `{R(c2,c3), R(c3,c4)}` — a clean 2-chain in the 5-chain data.
   Refinement worked.

4. **Refinement is bounded.**
   A graph consisting only of a 3-cycle (no chain) offers no clean
   2-chain anywhere. The corresponding unit test
   `refine_is_noop_when_no_clean_alternative` locks the behavior:
   refine returns the original representative unchanged after
   exhausting the budget. Users who need a guarantee can check
   `is_clean_subgraph` on the output.

5. **Composition with `discover_motifs` is straightforward.**
   `rs.refine_candidates(rs.discover_motifs(&disc_config), &refine_config)`
   is a one-liner. The RefinementConfig is small enough to pass
   inline. The two functions use separate RNG seeds (one for
   sampling, one for refinement) so the randomness is
   orthogonally controllable.

====================================================================
WHAT THIS ENABLES / WHAT IT DOES NOT
====================================================================

Enables:
  - Motif candidates carry clean representatives whenever the data
    supports them.
  - The future 0018 motif → pattern pipeline can call refine
    before name_pattern_instances and get correct ADR 0010
    canonical-recovery behavior for free.
  - Cross-run reproducibility of all sampling-based mechanisms.

Does NOT enable (still deferred):
  - Local edge-swap hill climbing. ADR 0017 explicitly chose
    targeted re-sampling; a future ADR could add swap-based
    refinement when a specific use case needs it.
  - Canonical-level refinement (drift to nearby canonicals with
    better score). Still out of scope.
  - Automatic motif naming. Caller still composes explicitly.

====================================================================
DECISION / NEXT
====================================================================

ADR 0017 is validated. The sample-score-refine loop is now
complete enough for 0018:

  discover_motifs(config_d)        # propose + score + select
    → refine_candidates(config_r)  # polish representatives
    → for each candidate:
         if canonical unseen in registry AND rep is clean:
             name_pattern_instances(&[rep])     # record as pattern

That is ADR 0018: the motif → pattern pipeline. It closes the
autonomous-abstraction loop — the system's own sampling proposes
structural types and its own cleanness check decides which ones
become first-class.
